        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/alexcrichton\">alexcrichton</a> added the wasm-proposal:component-model-async label to <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14576\">Issue #14576</a>.</p>",
        "id": 629607127,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791305955
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14576#issuecomment-6022888990\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14576\">issue #14576</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A related issue is that right now the runtime will only run sibling threads for a blocked sync task on the first switch, but after that it'll run anything. This is I believe all safe and sound and fine, but spec-incorrect. Some LLM details/summary is at <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/alexcrichton/26e1f262bfda51ab286765985184001d\">https://gist.github.com/alexcrichton/26e1f262bfda51ab286765985184001d</a></p>\n</blockquote>",
